# Gate step 1459-b5fh — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. cheatsheets/INDEX.md is generated and committed, so its bytes
# must not depend on the host. The policy crate used to delegate collation to
# an external sort, so glibc en_US, MSYS/Cygwin and C each gave a different
# order (and on Windows a bare sort ran System32's sort.exe). It now sorts in
# Rust by byte order. The fixture runs --check under LC_ALL=C and
# en_US.UTF-8 and pins podman-control-plane.md before podman.md.
# Pre-fix (trunk's INDEX): violation 1/3.
#
# The two other outputs sharing the helpers (the container-start stream order
# and the bundled-tier fetch key) read no locale and spawn nothing; the unit
# test no_external_sort_is_spawned pins that for the whole crate.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the cheatsheet INDEX is byte-ordered and locale-independent (1459-b5fh)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-cheatsheet-index-byte-order.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the cheatsheet INDEX order depends on the host locale again, or is stale (1459-b5fh); regenerate with scripts/regenerate-cheatsheet-index.sh and see which arm failed above"
STEP_OK="cheatsheet INDEX is byte-ordered under C and en_US.UTF-8"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="yolanda 2026-09-28 msys ok:cheatsheet-index-byte-order:3"
